        "mission_intent": "Subject: Full Specification Needed \u2014 COSO-Aligned Internal Control Framework Documentation\n\nTeam, as part of our annual regulatory readiness initiative, I need us to produce a comprehensive internal control specification document that fully aligns with the COSO Internal Control\u2014Integrated Framework, which as you know has been the broadly accepted standard since its original release in 1992 and remains the leading reference used worldwide for designing and evaluating internal control systems. The specification should address all five components of the framework\u2014control environment, risk assessment, control activities, information and communication, and monitoring activities\u2014and map each to our existing financial reporting processes across all business units. For each component, document the associated principles, identify the responsible process owners, and specify the evidence artifacts required to demonstrate operating effectiveness. The document must satisfy expectations consistent with SEC and PCAOB oversight standards, and it should be structured so that our external auditors at the Big Four firm can rely on it during the integrated audit. Please coordinate with the Chief Risk Officer's team and our compliance group to ensure enterprise risk considerations are incorporated. I'd like a draft ready for leadership review by end of next quarter, with a final version delivered no later than thirty days before our fiscal year-end audit kickoff. Use our existing GRC platform (ServiceNow IRM) as the system of record for control documentation and testing workflows.",
